-- Types seen: `payment.succeeded`, `payment.failed`, `payment.refunded`. Only the first is handled.
+- Types seen: `payment.succeeded`, `payment.failed`, `payment.refunded`. We handle `payment.succeeded` (paid, the stock leaves) and `payment.refunded` (refunded, the stock comes back if the order was paid); `payment.failed` is ignored.
+- Cancellation (`POST /orders/:id/cancel`): only a `pending` order, otherwise 409. Logic in `services/orders.js` (`cancelOrder`, `refundOrder`), shared by v1 and v2. The route is in v1 too, because v2 is not wired in and the feature must work now.
+- Known limit: the payment link stays valid after a cancellation. If the customer pays all the same, `payment.succeeded` moves the order to `paid` (the money is cashed); to refund by hand in PayFlux.
 - Signature: `X-Payflux-Signature` header, hex HMAC-SHA256 of the raw body, with the webhook secret. Verify on the body as it arrives, not on the reformatted JSON.
 - PayFlux doc, "Webhook delivery" (copied on 2026-03-15): "at least once" delivery. New attempt at +30 s, +5 min, +1 h, +6 h then +24 h as long as the answer is not a 2xx received within 5 s. An event already acknowledged may be redelivered. The event's `id` does not change from one delivery to the next.
 - The webhook URL is set in the PayFlux dashboard, Developers > Webhooks.
